The Python OpenAI client docs only describe routing precedence and environment fallback, not cross-model/provider failover: explicit Azure inputs or `OPENAI_API_KEY` are chosen first, then Azure env fallback, and `model=` overrides env vars ([python/packages/openai/agent_framework_openai/_chat_client.py:507-518](${LOCAL_PATH} [python/packages/openai/README.md:66-79](${LOCAL_PATH}

The repo’s retry sample retries `RateLimitError` on the same chat call with `tenacity`; it does not switch to a different model or provider ([python/samples/02-agents/auto_retry.py:116-173](${LOCAL_PATH}

If you need failover behavior, the repo points to chat middleware as the extension point for observing, modifying, and overriding model calls and handling failures ([python/samples/02-agents/middleware/README.md:9-13](${LOCAL_PATH} [python/samples/02-agents/middleware/exception_handling_with_middleware.py:19-25](${LOCAL_PATH}

- The browser keeps the thread/conversation id across turns: `Chat.razor` saves each response’s `ConversationId`, sends only the new messages after `statefulMessageCount`, and resets both on “New chat”. `AGUIChatClient` then moves that id into `agui_thread_id` for the request and strips `ConversationId` from yielded updates so the wrapper client doesn’t treat it as its own session state. [dotnet/samples/05-end-to-end/AGUIWebChat/Client/Components/Pages/Chat/Chat.razor:54-64](${LOCAL_PATH} [dotnet/src/Microsoft.Agents.AI.AGUI/AGUIChatClient.cs:92-104](${LOCAL_PATH} [dotnet/src/Microsoft.Agents.AI.AGUI/AGUIChatClient.cs:251-275](${LOCAL_PATH}

- On the server, `MapAGUI` uses `input.ThreadId` (or generates one), calls `hostAgent.GetOrCreateSessionAsync(threadId)`, and saves the session after the streamed run finishes. Restoration happens through a keyed `AgentSessionStore`: `WithInMemorySessionStore()` registers `InMemoryAgentSessionStore`, which reloads a serialized session by `<agentId>:<conversationId>`; if no keyed store exists, `MapAGUI` falls back to `NoopAgentSessionStore`. [dotnet/src/Microsoft.Agents.AI.Hosting.AGUI.AspNetCore/AGUIEndpointRouteBuilderExtensions.cs:85-156](${LOCAL_PATH} [dotnet/src/Microsoft.Agents.AI.Hosting/HostedAgentBuilderExtensions.cs:20-23](${LOCAL_PATH} [dotnet/src/Microsoft.Agents.AI.Hosting/Local/InMemoryAgentSessionStore.cs:33-49](${LOCAL_PATH}

- Streaming is converted into AG-UI events, and mixed tool batches are split so client/browser tools and server tools do not get conflated. `FilterServerToolsFromMixedToolInvocationsAsync` removes server tools from a `ToolCalls` batch when both kinds are present, and `AGUIChatClient` wraps server-only function calls in `ServerFunctionCallContent` while preserving client tool calls via `agui_thread_id`, so the browser-side `FunctionInvokingChatClient` only executes the client tools. [dotnet/src/Microsoft.Agents.AI.Hosting.AGUI.AspNetCore/AGUIChatResponseUpdateStreamExtensions.cs:14-88](${LOCAL_PATH} [dotnet/src/Microsoft.Agents.AI.AGUI/AGUIChatClient.cs:251-275](${LOCAL_PATH}
